{
 "about": "How a scalar placeholder enters a filter predicate when its value holds characters the filter dialects reserve. ${resourceType} is the scalar a case can fill with any text: each case loads a set whose target is resourceType == '<type>' for a type that holds such characters, and one ALLOW rule on LIST whose rsql, sql, mongodb and querydsl predicates each read ${resourceType} unquoted. The filter request asks for that type; the check beside it, on LIST, says whether the set applies to the type at all. The goldens so far put only letters, digits and _ into a scalar placeholder, and show it unquoted.",
 "resourceTypePrefix": "PARITY_SUITE_R28T_",
 "pins": {},
 "pips": {},
